description:
Change under review: let users save dashboard preferences. Added files are shown in full; the last file is existing, unchanged code shown for context.

`src/prefs/merge.ts` (added):
```ts
1 type Json = Record<string, unknown>;
2
3 export function deepMerge(target: Json, source: Json): Json {
4   for (const key in source) {
5     const value = source[key];
6     if (value !== null && typeof value === "object" && !Array.isArray(value)) {
7       target[key] = deepMerge((target[key] as Json) ?? {}, value as Json);
8     } else {
9       target[key] = value;
10     }
11   }
12   return target;
13 }
```

`src/routes/prefs.ts` (added):
```ts
1 import { requireSession } from "../auth/session.js";
2 import { deepMerge } from "../prefs/merge.js";
3 import { loadPrefs, storePrefs } from "../prefs/store.js";
4
5 export const savePrefs = requireSession(async (req) => {
6   const patch = await req.json();
7   const prefs = deepMerge(await loadPrefs(req.session.userId), patch);
8   await storePrefs(req.session.userId, prefs);
9   return Response.json(prefs);
10 });
```

`src/auth/roles.ts` (unchanged, lines 10-13):
```ts
10 export function isAdmin(user: User): boolean {
11   const flags: Record<string, unknown> = user.flags ?? {};
12   return flags.admin === true;
13 }
```

`loadPrefs` returns a plain object parsed from the stored JSON. Every tenant of the service is served by the same long-running server process. Existing middleware enforces CSRF protection on every state-changing route: the session cookie is `SameSite=Strict`, and a request without a valid `X-CSRF-Token` header is rejected.
